# Local working files — never committed, never shared.
#
# Anything worth keeping but not worth releasing goes here: scratch scripts,
# run artifacts, debugging notebooks, superseded plans, client configs. One
# entry, true in advance. This directory exists so that no future scratch file
# needs its own line in this file — the pattern that preceded it accumulated a
# dozen individually-named paths, each added only after the file had already
# appeared, and a commit once swept in sixteen files in the gap before the next
# line was written.
.local/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.venv/
build/
dist/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.idea/
.claude/
.serena/
.impeccable/
.superpowers/
CLAUDE.md

# Editor and OS droppings. .DS_Store is caught by most developers' global
# ignore file; it is repeated here so the repo does not depend on that.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# Credentials. The only file here that is dangerous rather than merely untidy.
config/config.ini
# The installation's settings. The repo ships config/settings.ini.example instead.
config/settings.ini

# Runtime output directories the product itself creates, relative to the working
# directory: results/ (core.py RESULT_PATH), cube-configs/ and exports/ (the ui.py
# defaults for saved cube configs and Sync Order exports; Settings can move both)
# and logs/ (core.py log path). They are working state, not scratch, so they stay
# where the code expects them rather than moving under .local/.
results/
cube-configs/
exports/
logs/
*.log

# mkdocs build output. Note this is NOT ./site — site/homepage is the tracked
# React landing page, and mkdocs is configured with site_dir: mkdocs_site to
# keep the two apart.
mkdocs_site/

# Internal planning, not part of the published documentation set.
docs/superpowers/
docs/plans/
docs/*.docx
